Hi Ian,

Thanks for the response! I have been considering scaling up my covariate rasters, and that will be what I test out next - see how scaling affects the estimated relationships, density, etc.

I think I see what was going wrong in my thought process - I've been almost thinking of this in terms of habitat use or preference, rather than population densities, which operate and are affected at greater scales. It makes sense to average conditions out over a mask cell because what I really want to know is what population density of hares is supported by a certain understory density (or whatever forest structure attribute).

