I'm not sure what is tripping you up. The expected value is a property of a statistical distribution. In this case it refers to what you might call the average distance moved (when habitat is not constraining). See section 2.7 of Efford & Schofield 2022 <https://besjournals.onlinelibrary.wiley.com/doi/10.1111/2041-210X.13947>.
Murray

